Lane A owns the save schema. Do not apply this from lane D.

The Hall of Fame plan keeps an in-memory party record (species, level, species
name) and then rolls the credits and returns to the title without saving.
pokered's HallOfFamePC also writes that record, saves, resets the Indigo
Plateau event range through EVENT_LANCES_ROOM_LOCK_DOOR, and sets the last
blackout map to PALLET_TOWN. SessionCodec.object() rejects an unknown
hallOfFame field, so the record cannot persist yet.

tools/tests/test_lane_d_endgame.py marks
test_save_schema_keeps_a_hall_of_fame_record as an expected failure until the
allowlist below is accepted and a decoder for the record is added.

--- a/Source/domain/sessionCodec.lua
+++ b/Source/domain/sessionCodec.lua
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ local function normalize(record,deps)
     checkpoint()
     object(data,{version=true,pokemonEncoding=true,title=true,intro=true,questFlags=true,trainerFlags=true,pokedex=true,
-        location=true,checkpoint=true,world=true,party=true,storage=true,inventory=true,rng=true,worldMotion=true,itemStorage=true,fieldWorld=true,daycare=true,fieldTravel=true,safari=true,coins=true})
+        location=true,checkpoint=true,world=true,party=true,storage=true,inventory=true,rng=true,worldMotion=true,itemStorage=true,fieldWorld=true,daycare=true,fieldTravel=true,safari=true,coins=true,hallOfFame=true})
     assert((data.version==1 or data.version==2 or data.version==3 or data.version==SessionCodec.VERSION) and data.pokemonEncoding==SessionCodec.POKEMON_ENCODING,"unsupported-session-version-or-Pokemon-encoding")
